        <text class="tt9-label" x="39" y="76" text-anchor="middle">OLD SESSION</text>
        <text class="tt9-note" x="39" y="88" text-anchor="middle">WEEKS EARLIER</text>
        <text class="tt9-note" x="86" y="80">IDENTICAL KEY SET</text>

        <rect class="tt9-panel" x="1" y="98" width="258" height="18" rx="2" aria-hidden="true" />
        <text class="tt9-label" x="130" y="111" text-anchor="middle">INSTRUMENT, NOT DRIFT</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="fig-what">
          The sweep sat between the record and the answer, and it reported
          nothing found. A session recorded weeks earlier carried the identical
          key set, so the verdict is the instrument and not vendor drift.
        </span>
        <span class="fig-limit">
          The plate carries no count; both counts are cited figures, so they
          stay in the prose below with their design-document reference.
