    <h2 id="what-it-demonstrates">What it demonstrates</h2>
    <p>
      The rest of this record is a system I built with agents. This is the
      instrument I built to watch them. The honesty rule is one sentence: a
      gauge may not render a number nobody measured. Golden files enforce that
      rule, not intent, because intent does not fail a build.
    </p>
    <p>
      I refused a list of features outright, and each one would have required an
      invented number. Every refusal is a file you can read, with the argument
      still attached.
    </p>
    <p>
      When my own instrument was the thing that was wrong, the correction went
      into the record next to the claim it broke. Both times the wrong answer
      arrived as an absence and not as an error. That is the failure mode this
      product is least able to see in itself. Every sentence above resolves to a
      file you can open.
    </p>
